{"title":"Career roadmap · Archaeologist","role":"Archaeologist","summary":"An Archaeologist studies past human societies through material evidence such as archaeological sites, monuments, artefacts, inscriptions, ceramics, coins, tools, architecture and environmental remains. A BA in History provides a strong foundation in chronology, historiography, political and social history, cultural development and source analysis, but professional archaeology generally requires specialised postgraduate study and field training.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"An Archaeologist studies past human societies through material evidence such as archaeological sites, monuments, artefacts, inscriptions, ceramics, coins, tools, architecture and environmental remains. A BA in History provides a strong foundation in chronology, historiography, political and social history, cultural development and source analysis, but professional archaeology generally requires specialised postgraduate study and field training."},{"type":"p","text":"For a History graduate, the strongest pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["History","Archaeology/Heritage PG","Fieldwork","Archaeological specialisation","Research/Heritage career"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Undergraduate"},{"text":"Archaeology Intern, Heritage Research Intern"},{"text":"Field exposure and documentation"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Archaeological Research Assistant, Field Assistant"},{"text":"Surveys, excavation support, documentation"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Archaeologist, Archaeological Researcher"},{"text":"Fieldwork, artefact/site analysis"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Field Archaeologist, Underwater Archaeologist, Archaeobotanist, Bioarchaeologist"},{"text":"Specialised research"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Archaeologist, Project Archaeologist"},{"text":"Excavation and project leadership"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Archaeological Project Director, Heritage Specialist"},{"text":"Large projects and heritage management"}],[{"text":"Academic"},{"text":"Archaeology Researcher, Lecturer, Professor"},{"text":"Research and teaching"}],[{"text":"Government"},{"text":"Archaeological Officer / Specialist roles"},{"text":"Public archaeology and heritage"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Heritage/Archaeology Programme Head"},{"text":"Institutional and programme leadership"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"The exact eligibility for government archaeology posts varies by organisation and notification. A BA History alone should not be presented as sufficient for specialist archaeologist positions."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During BA History","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Historical Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Core knowledge"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ancient Indian history"},{"text":"Medieval Indian history"},{"text":"Modern Indian history"},{"text":"World history"},{"text":"Cultural history"},{"text":"Historiography"},{"text":"Historical geography"},{"text":"Political and social institutions"},{"text":"Introduction to archaeology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start developing archaeological awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Archaeological sites"},{"text":"Material culture"},{"text":"Stratigraphy"},{"text":"Artefacts"},{"text":"Monuments"},{"text":"Inscriptions"},{"text":"Coins"},{"text":"Ceramics"},{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"Heritage conservation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic reading"},{"text":"Source criticism"},{"text":"Bibliographic research"},{"text":"Note-taking"},{"text":"Citation"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Historical interp